# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# Three test files were CRLF while the other 84 were LF, and the build recipe
# in each header comment uses backslash continuations. A backslash followed by
# CR is not a continuation to bash, so every line of the command ran as a
# separate command -- and tests/run_all.sh reported it as "compile error",
# pointing at the compiler, which was never involved. Two tests were red for a
# long time over a line ending.
#
# run_all.sh now strips CR defensively; this stops the situation arising.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.iso  binary
*.img  binary
*.bin  binary
# The initrd (sidecars.cpio) is a binary newc archive: its payload images
# legitimately contain 0x0D bytes, and text=auto must never line-convert it
# on checkout/commit. Marked binary so script_conventions_check.sh skips the
# CR-byte scan (same rule as *.png/*.iso above).
*.cpio binary
# The .flat probe payload and the E7 census-candidate ELF are byte-exact
# toolchain outputs (objcopy / ld) whose MACHINE bytes legitimately contain
# 0x0D; text=auto must never line-convert them, and
# script_conventions_check.sh's CR scan skips whatever carries the
# `binary` attribute — same rule as *.cpio above.
*.flat binary
*.elf binary
# The e7_* evidence logs are RAW serial captures: the UART emits CRLF and
# the coalesced stream carries NUL bytes, so they are byte evidence, not
# source text — text=auto would refuse to line-convert them anyway (NUL
# detection), and the CR scan skips whatever carries `binary` — same rule
# as *.cpio above.
evidence/*.log binary
vendor/** -text -diff
